{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 121, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 2 is already none, removing edge 1 leaves node 2 with no input, so edge 5 carries nothing and the cell loses capacity (exps 50, 52 versus 49, 51)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is already none, removing edge 2 leaves node 2 with no input, so edge 5 is dead; otherwise node 2 still gets input from edge 1."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 none, removing edge 0 leaves both node 1 and node 2 with no input, so only edge 3 reaches the output (exps 18, 19 versus 15-17)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 already none, removing edge 5 leaves edge 3 as the only input to the output (exp 99 versus 98)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 already none, removing edge 4 leaves edge 3 as the only input to the output, so all deep processing is lost."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is none, removing edge 3 makes the output depend only on node 2, so the cell can become nearly disconnected (exp 39)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is none, removing edge 3 leaves only edge 4, a single input to the output, which hurts badly (exp 39 versus 38, 41)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a missing edge 0 into a skip connection gives node 1 an input again, which revives edges 2 and 4 (exp 48), a much bigger gain than replacing a convolution with skip (exp 44)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling on edge 5 with a 3x3 convolution adds learnable capacity at the output, which helps more than replacing a skip connection (exps 5, 6 versus 1-4)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the 3x3 convolution on edge 5 with pooling throws away the main learnable path into the output, which hurts more than replacing a skip connection (exps 32, 34, 35 versus 33)."}], "tok": 17756, "bad": 1, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "av